---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Online Ruler"
  description="Privacy policy for the Online Ruler tool detailing client-side data handling and local execution."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 space-y-6 text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-sm leading-relaxed">
    <header class="space-y-1">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)]">Effective Date: October 19, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">1. Client-Side Processing Commitment</h2>
      <p>
        Online Ruler operates entirely within your web browser. All geometric calculations, degree measurements, image uploads, and live camera streams are executed locally on your client hardware. We do not store, process, or transmit your images or camera feeds to external servers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">2. Camera & Photo Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        When you enable the camera feature, the application requests temporary access via your browser’s standard MediaDevices API. This video stream exists solely in memory during your active session. Revoking camera permission or closing the browser tab terminates the stream immediately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">3. Cookies & CDN Logs</h2>
      <p>
        Our CDN provider (Cloudflare) records basic connection logs including IP address, browser type, and access timestamps to protect against denial-of-service attacks. Third-party advertising partners like Google may use cookies to serve relevant ads. You can opt out via your browser settings or Google Ad Settings.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>
